TPT-Wasm is an independent Rust implementation of WebAssembly.
It is not a fork, derivative, or copy of any existing WebAssembly runtime.

The implementation is based on the following public specifications:
  - WebAssembly Core Specification, W3C (https://webassembly.github.io/spec/)
  - WebAssembly WASI Specification (https://wasi.dev/)
  - WebAssembly Component Model Specification (https://component-model.bytecodealliance.org/)

The WebAssembly specification test suite is used for interoperability testing only
and is not incorporated into the distributed software.

Third-party Rust crates used as dependencies retain their own copyright notices
and license terms. See docs/licensing/provenance.md for the dependency provenance
record, and the output of `cargo deny` / `cargo metadata` for the full list.

No implementation code from external WebAssembly runtimes (Wasmtime, Wasmer,
WasmEdge, WAMR, or others) has been incorporated into this project.
